          "y": 16,
          "width": 96,
          "line_height": 9,
          "text": "Recognition starts from the gyromancy:mana effect layer. ManaPixelDetector does not treat every opaque color as a stroke; visible pixels without the mana effect are ignored."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• The ink's manaValue is written to every covered brush pixel.\n• Additional effectKeys leave room for elemental inks, markers, and filters."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• Erasing must clear both color and effects or visual and recognition state diverge."
    },
